Title: Swap deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash:free → deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash (paid) in journal set
Created: 2026-05-20
Author: claude
Closed: autoclosed — PR #349 (code) + PR #360 (data)

--- log ---
2026-05-20T20:50Z claude created — discovered during 0181 execution. Free-tier route caps completion at 4096 tokens regardless of requested max_tokens=32768.

2026-05-20T22:48Z HDMX-coding-agent closed — autoclosed — PR #349 (code) + PR #360 (data)
--- body ---
## Context

During the 0181 sweep (run by a concurrent agent in worktree
`agent-ad937f289caeac791`, branch built off PR #346 / commit fa89de5),
the `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash:free` model produced records with
`finish_reason=length` at **exactly 4096 completion tokens** despite the
sweep config's `max_tokens=32768`:

```
deepseek-v4-flash-free-run3.json: finish=length comp_tokens=4096 max_tokens=32768
deepseek-v4-flash-free-run4.json: finish=length comp_tokens=4096 max_tokens=32768
```

(Both records under `outputs/ablation/direct/p1_base/` in that worktree.)

OpenRouter `/api/v1/models` metadata for the free route reports
`max_completion_tokens=384000`, but the **provider-side per-call output
cap on the `:free` tier is empirically 4096**. The cap is not configurable
from our side. Records under the free tier are systematically truncated
mid-table.

The paid variant `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` (no `:free` suffix) has
`max_completion_tokens=None` (no cap) per OpenRouter metadata. Pricing
verified 2026-05-20:

```
deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash      ctx=1048576  $0.112/Mtok in  $0.224/Mtok out  cache_read=$0.022/Mtok
```

Architecture: MoE, 284B total / 13B active, 1M-token context. Same
family as the free variant; the only difference is the output cap.

Expected sweep cost for 5 reps × ~8K-10K output tokens ≈ **$0.01 total**.

## Decision

**Replace, not augment.** Drop `:free`; add paid. The two are the same
model — there's no scientific reason to keep both in the journal set,
and the free-tier truncation produces unusable data for the F1 evaluation.
Journal set stays at 17 models.

## Impact

- **0181 (in flight)**: the 2 `:free` records already produced are
  truncated and should be discarded. After 0182 lands, those 5 reps need
  re-running against the paid slug.
- **0182 follow-up sweep**: 5 reps × $0.002 each = ~$0.01 total. Can be
  appended to 0181's run output dir; `should_skip` won't help because
  the slug changes (free→paid produces different output filenames:
  `deepseek-v4-flash-free-run*.json` vs `deepseek-v4-flash-run*.json`).
  The 2 stale `:free` records should be deleted, not left as orphans
  in the output dir.
- **Experiment 2 / Wave 2 (SOTA agents)**: no impact — those tickets use
  different model pins.
- **Manuscript (0178)**: annex must note the model-set chain
  0175 → 0180 (Opus/Qwen) → 0182 (DeepSeek), and that the DeepSeek
  Flash data point in the final dataset is from the paid route.

## Actions

1. **models.yaml**: add `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` (paid) entry with
   verified prices from OpenRouter `/api/v1/models` (see above).
   Architecture: MoE; country: CN; size_class: same tier as the
   existing `:free` entry; context_window: 1048576. Mirror the YAML
   shape of the adjacent `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro` entry.

2. **models.yaml**: do NOT delete the `:free` entry (per project policy
   "Never delete entries — comment out with date and reason"). Comment
   it out with a `# Removed YYYY-MM-DD: output capped at 4K tokens by
   provider, truncates the inventory-table task. See ticket 0182.`

3. **experiments.toml `[sets.modelset_ablation_journal]`**: replace
   `"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash:free"` with `"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"`.
   Set size stays 17.

4. **measurements.jsonl hygiene**: delete the 2 `:free` records under
   `outputs/ablation/direct/p1_base/deepseek-v4-flash-free-run{3,4}.json`
   (the concurrent agent's worktree) before the post-0181 rebuild.
   If 0181 has already completed and ingested the truncated records,
   `make rebuild-measurements` after deletion drops them cleanly.

5. **Re-run the 5 deepseek-flash reps** against the paid slug. Either
   as part of 0181's drain (if 0181 hasn't completed yet) or as a tiny
   follow-up sweep targeting only this one model. Total cost ~$0.01.

6. Note in 0181's closing log entry that the DeepSeek Flash reps came
   from the paid slug per 0182, not the free slug as originally listed
   in PR #341.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `models.yaml` has new `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` entry, prices
      verified against OpenRouter
- [ ] `models.yaml` `:free` entry commented out with date + reason
- [ ] `experiments.toml` journal set replaces `:free` with paid slug;
      still 17 model_ids total
- [ ] 2 stale `:free` records deleted from outputs/p1_base/
- [ ] 5 paid-route reps run; records present in
      `outputs/ablation/direct/p1_base/deepseek-v4-flash-run{1..5}.json`
      with `finish_reason!=length` (or, if length, with the new
      `max_tokens=32768` actually consumed, not the 4096 cap)
- [ ] `measurements.jsonl` rebuilt; the 5 paid-route records appear
      under `prompt_version="p1_base"` and `seed=42`
- [ ] 0181 closing log entry references 0182
- [ ] 0178 manuscript annex notes the chain

## Notes

- 0181 (in flight) is unaware of this; the concurrent agent will land
  the 80 non-DeepSeek-flash records cleanly and the 5 truncated free-tier
  records can be replaced after the fact. No need to halt 0181.
- The `:free` route's 4096 cap is undocumented in OpenRouter's model
  metadata; this is a footgun other agents may hit. Worth a separate
  note in `experiments/models.yaml`'s header policy (or a tiny test that
  greps free-route entries and warns).
- DeepSeek V3.2 (also in the registry, also free-route) is not in the
  journal set — no action needed for it here.
